  "carve": {
   "heightAboveRim": 1.1,
   "profileNotes": "PRS \"shallow violin\" carve on a maple top over a flat mahogany back. Total depth ~4.6 cm at the bridge (Guitar World measured \"a shade over 46 mm\"), rim ~3.5 cm (estimated). Flat ledge along the whole edge (see ledgeWidths / carveStartOutline), then a smooth convex rise to a broad crown on the centerline between the bridge and bridge pickup (y 15-20); the top stays fairly high toward the neck (~0.6 above rim at the neck joint) but is carved down strongly into both horns (drawing contour lines at bass horn x -10..-4 y 36-44 and treble horn x 3.7..10.8 y 33-38). Cross sections: crown on x=0, falling symmetrically to the ledge line; lower bout slope is gentle (reaches ~0.5 at 5 cm from the ledge).",
   "recurveNotes": "No dish below rim level. Ledge ~1.1 cm wide (flat, natural-maple edge), then a short concave transition (~1.0-1.5 cm) into the convex arch. Treble cutaway additionally has a steep scoop that exposes natural wood from the cutaway edge inward ~1.5-2.5 cm (visible in product photos).",
