 "notes": "All geometry traced from the official PRS SE Custom 24 straight-on photo, treated as orthographic. Scale 34.52 px/cm from a least-squares fit of all 24 frets (validated: nut width 4.296 vs 4.286 published, neck width at 24th fret 5.705 vs 5.715). Body measured 32.50 x 44.55 cm (12.80 x 17.54 in); published/owner figures for USA CU24 range 12 7/8-13 x 17 1/2-17 3/4 in (tape over the carve reads larger); residual perspective uncertainty ~0.5%. Outline under the fretboard (between the neck-edge junctions) is interpolated. Headstock outline measured in the photo and divided by cos(10 deg) along y for the headstock pitch; tuner-button occlusions bridged by smooth interpolation. saddleLineY is nominal (nutY - 63.5); actual saddle crowns sit 0.1-0.4 cm behind it (compensation). Carve heights and rim thickness are estimates; the ledge line is from a USA drawing. SE bodies share the Custom 24 outline; photo vs USA drawing max deviation 3.4 mm (treble horn)."
}